nst DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 100;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40, rune: 25, moonstone: 25,\n};\n// types...\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const items = (scenario as ScenarioInput).steps[0].items ?? [];\n  const basePremium = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumFor(item as Item), 0);\n  return { results: [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD }] };\n};\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n- Constants: 10 (`5`, `100`, six map values, `0`, `\"\"`) → 10\n- Bindings: 9 (`PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD`, `DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD`, `BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD`, `item`, `scenario`, `items`, `basePremium`, `sum`, `item`) → 9\n- Invocations: 4 (`reduce`, `basePremiumFor`, two `+`) → 8\n- Conditionals: 0 → 0\n- Loops: 1 (`reduce`) → 5\n- Assignments: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass: 32**\n\n## Refactored Code Mass (after)\n\n```ts\nconst PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD = 5;\nconst UNKNOWN_TYPE_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 100;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40, rune: 25, moonstone: 25,\n};\n// types...\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? UNKNOWN_TYPE_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst sumBasePremiums = (items: unknown[]): number =>\n  items.reduce<number>((sum, rawItem) => sum + basePremiumFor(rawItem as Item), 0);\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const items = (scenario as ScenarioInput).steps[0].items ?? [];\n  const basePremium = sumBasePremiums(items);\n  return { results: [{ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD }] };\n};\n```\n\nComponent count:\n\n- Constants: 10 → 10\n- Bindings: 10 (`PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD`, `UNKNOWN_TYPE_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD`, `BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD`, `item`, `items` (helper param), `sum`, `rawItem`, `scenario`, `items` (local), `basePremium`) → 10\n- Invocations: 5 (`reduce`, `basePremiumFor`, two `+`, `sumBasePremiums`) → 10\n- Conditionals: 0 → 0\n- Loops: 1 → 5\n- Assignments: 0 → 0\n\n**Total Mass: 35**  \n**Mass Change: 32 → 35 (+3)**\n\n## Simple Design Rule Evaluation\n\n1. **Tests pass** — all 6 active tests pass; 39 tests remain todo.\n2. **Reveals intent** — improved:\n   - Renamed `DEFAULT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD` → `UNKNOWN_TYPE_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD`.\n   - Renamed `calculateBasePremium` → `sumBasePremiums`.\n   - Extracted the premium-summing logic so `processScenario` reads as “get items, sum base premiums, add fee.”\n   - Added explicit `reduce<number>` generic to make the accumulator type obvious and satisfy strict TypeScript inference.\n3. **No duplication** — no duplicated logic found.\n4. **Fewest elements** — initially extracted `itemsFromScenario`, then removed it after deciding the one-line extraction in `processScenario` was clearer and avoided an unnecessary abstraction.\n\n## Notes\n\n- I attempted to drop the `?? \"\"` fallback in `basePremiumFor`, but TypeScript’s strict index signature requires a string key, so the fallback is needed for type-correctness.\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, and `pnpm test` passes.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n- **Refactoring**: Extracted `sumBasePremiums`, renamed constants/functions for clarity, added explicit `reduce<number>` type.\n- **Mass Change**: 32 → 35 (+3); acceptable because Rule 2 (intent) trumps mass.\n- **Tests**: All passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent Green phase: Added rune and moonstone base premiums 25 G to loo