urcharges + loyaltyDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\nreturn { results: [{ premium }] };\n```\n\n| Component   | Count | Mass |\n|-------------|-------|------|\n| Constants   | 1     | 1    |\n| Bindings    | 7     | 7    |\n| Invocations | 1     | 2    |\n| Conditionals| 1     | 4    |\n| Loops       | 0     | 0    |\n| Assignments | 0     | 0    |\n| **Total**   |       | **14** |\n\n**Mass Change:** `20 → 14` (delta `-6`)\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n1. **Naming (Rule 2)**: Renamed `policyWideModifierRateFor` → `loyaltyDiscountRateFor` and `policyWideModifier` → `loyaltyDiscount` to reveal intent.\n2. **Simplification / Fewer Elements (Rule 4)**: Replaced the mutable `let rate` and `if` block with a single ternary expression, removing an assignment and a binding.\n3. **Clarity (Rule 2)**: Extracted the final premium calculation into a named `premium` variable before returning.\n\n## Tests\n\n```\npnpm test\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (45 tests | 28 skipped)\nTests  17 passed | 28 todo (45)\n```\n\nAll 17 passing tests remain green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added policy-wide loyalty discount applied to policy base\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: Added policy-wide loyalty discount applied to policy base\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784923721839},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need respond to user. User is passing refactor subagent task. The instructions say use subagent tool for refactor. But the user is already asking us as refactor agent? Wait: In this harness, the assistant may have custom tools including subagent? The available functions list only read/write/edit/bash/grep/find/ls. There's no subagent tool. The user message seems to be a task to perform refactoring as a subagent. We are the refactor agent. Need follow refactor process from system instructions: MUST attempt at least one refactoring, evaluate naming first, calculate APP mass before and after, apply simple design rules in priority, keep tests green, document decisions.\n\nWe need inspect files: src/claim-office.spec.ts and src/claim-office.ts. Also maybe project setup. Need read them. Then run tests to ensure green. Then evaluate code, make refactoring attempt, run tests.\n\nWe must keep all tests green. Need calculate mass before and after. Need make at least one improvement. We should explore code. Use read tool.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":81,"output":248,"cacheRead":5568,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":210,"totalTokens":5897,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784923721860,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-93ea2daa-fb8d-4ad4-9e19-08670c65d79a","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD = 5;\nconst UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 100;\nconst COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 25;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\ntype Customer = {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Array<{ items?: unknown[] }>;\n};\n\ntype Item = {\n  type?: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n};\n\ntype PremiumBreakdown = {\n  policyBase: number;\n  itemSurcharges: number;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: Item, basePremium: number): number => {\n  let rate = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) rate += CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    rate += HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  }\n  return basePremium * rate;\n};\n\nconst componentBasePremiumForCount = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK\n    ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst premiumBreakdownForItems = (items: Item[]): PremiumBreakdown => {\n  const componentCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const type = item.type ?? \"\";\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(type, (componentCounts.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n      policyBase += base;\n      itemSurcharges += itemSurchargeFor(item, base);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const count of componentCounts.values()) {\n    policyBase += componentBasePremiumForCount(count);\n  }\n\n  return { policyBase, itemSurcharges };\n};\n\nconst policyWideModifierRateFor = (customer: Customer): number => {\n  let rate = 0;\n  if (customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD) rate -= LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  return rate;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const input = scenario as ScenarioInput;\n  const items = input.steps[0].items ?? [];\n  const customer = input.customer;\n  const { policyBase, itemSurcharges } = premiumBreakdownForItems(items as Item[]);\n  const policyWideModifier = policyBase * policyWideModifierRateFor(customer);\n  return { results: [{ premium: policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyWideModifier + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD }] };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923724340},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // Empty / simplest cases\n  it(\"should return premium 5 G for an empty item list -- only processing fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 105 G for a single plain sword -- 100 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 105 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 65 G for a single plain amulet -- 60 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 85 G for a single plain staff -- 80 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 85 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 45 G for a single plain potion -- 40 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 45 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 30 G for a single component -- 25 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 30 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Component blocks\n  it(\"should return premium 55 G for two runes -- 50 base + 5 fee (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 55 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 65 G for three runes -- 60 block base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 105 G for four runes -- 100 base + 5 fee (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 105 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 180 G for seven runes -- 175 base + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 180 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Alike components\n  it(\"should return premium 80 G for two runes and one moonstone -- 75 base + 5 fee (no block)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 80 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should return premium 125 G for three runes and three moonstones -- 120 block base + 5 fee (two blocks)\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"rune\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n            { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 125 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Item modifiers\n  it(\"should add 50% curse surcharge to a cursed sword -- premium 155 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 155 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should add 30% high-enchantment surcharge to an enchantment-5 sword -- premium 135 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 135 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should add 30% high-enchantment surcharge to an enchantment-5 amulet -- premium 83 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", enchantment: 5 }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 83 }] });\n  });\n  it(\"should apply both curse and high-enchantment surcharges -- premium 185 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }],\n        },\n      ],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 185 }] });\n  });\n\n  // Customer modifiers\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for a customer with exactly 2 years -- premium 85 G\", () => {\n    const result = processScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }],\n    });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 85 }] });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should apply 10% first-insurance surcharge for a new customer -- premium 110 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount -- premium 89 G\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item -- premium 210 G before fee\");\n\n  // Modifier thresholds\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years with MHPCO\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at exactly enchantment 5\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply both curse and high-enchantment surcharges when both conditions hold\");\n\n  // Integration examples\n  it.todo(\"should compute newcomer with a cursed steel enchantment-3 sword -- premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute long-standing customer's second contract with cursed steel enchantment-7 sword -- premium 160 G\");\n\n  // Claim: deductible and standard reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 400 G for a regular steel enchantment-3 sword damaged 500 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should pay out 100 G for a rune damaged 200 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply deductible once per damaged item in a multi-item incident\");\n\n  // Claim: special reimbursement clauses\n  it.todo(\"should reimburse enchantment-8 damage at 50% then deductible -- 400 G for 1000 G damage\");\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse dragon-material damage then deductible -- 900 G for 1000 G damage\");\n  it.todo(\"should let high-enchantment 50% rule win over dragon material for enchantment 9 -- 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should use dragon material only when enchantment is below 8 -- 700 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should use high-enchantment only on non-dragon steel -- 400 G\");\n\n  // Claim: multiple items and caps\n  it.todo(\"should track policy insurance sum and cap for two swords -- cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should treat each damage entry as separate with its own deductible for two swords\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject a claim when damages exceed insured count for a type\");\n  it.todo(\"should cap total payout at twice the insurance sum\");\n  it.todo(\"should reduce payout to remaining cap on second claim -- 600 G remaining\");\n  it.todo(\"should base cap on unmodified insurance value ignoring premium modifiers\");\n  it.todo(\"should not let component block discount affect insurance sum -- cap 2000 G\");\n\n  // Rounding\n  it.todo(\"should round a 197.5 G premium up to 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round a 350.5 G payout down to 350 G\");\n\n  // Error cases\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for unknown item type in quote\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for unknown item type in claim\");\n  it.todo(\"should exit with non-zero status for negative damage amount\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923724340},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need refactor the implementation while keeping tests green. The implementation is in src/claim-office.ts. We need attempt at least one refactoring. Let's run tests first to see all 17 pass. Then evaluate naming, duplication, etc. Need calculate APP mass before and after.\n\nPotential refactor improvements:\n- Naming: Function `processScenario` maybe fine. `policyWideModifierRateFor` returns rate which is discount only; maybe name could be `loyaltyDiscountRateFor` since it only applies loyalty discount. But spec has other customer modifiers: first-insurance surcharge, follow-up contract discount. Currently only loyalty implemented. But name `policyWideModifierRateFor` maybe too generic. Since it only returns loyalty discount, maybe rename to `loyaltyDiscountRateFor` to reveal intent. However tests will still pass.\n- Naming: `basePremiumForItem` maybe okay. `componentBasePremiumForCount` reveals. `premiumBreakdownForItems` okay.\n- Duplication: constants grouped at top. No much duplication.\n- In `premiumBreakdownForItems`, there is a loop that separates component items from non-component items, counts components. Could extract functions or simplify. The variable `type` repeated maybe. `policyWideModifierRateFor` uses `let rate = 0` pattern similar to `itemSurchargeFor`. Could extract a helper? Not necessary.\n- In `processScenario`, the final expression is long: `policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyWideModifier + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD`. Could introduce an explaining variable `premium` to clarify. But may not lower mass.\n- Could use early return and remove `let rate = 0`. For `itemSurchargeFor`, we can compute rate with conditional expressio