st insurance 0, fee 5. -> 5. Unchanged.\n- Test 2 (sword): 100 + 10 + 5 = 115. Description: \"100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\"\n- Test 3 (amulet): 60 + 6 + 5 = 71.\n- Test 4 (staff): 80 + 8 + 5 = 93.\n- Test 5 (potion): 40 + 4 + 5 = 49.\n- Test 6 (rune): 25 + 2.5 + 5 = 32.5 -> ceil 33.\n- Test 7 (2 runes): 50 + 5 + 5 = 60.\n- Test 8 (3 runes block): 60 + 6 + 5 = 71.\n- Test 9 (4 runes): 100 + 10 + 5 = 115.\n- Test 10 (7 runes): 175 + 17.5 + 5 = 197.5 -> ceil 198.\n- Test 11 (2 runes + 1 moonstone): 75 + 7.5 + 5 = 87.5 -> ceil 88.\n- Test 12 (3 runes + 3 moonstones): 120 + 12 + 5 = 137.\n- Test 13 (cursed sword): 100 + 50 + 10 + 5 = 165.\n- Test 14 (enchantment sword): 100 + 30 + 10 + 5 = 145.\n- Test 15 (enchantment amulet): 60 + 18 + 6 + 5 = 89.\n- Test 16 (both): 100 + 80 + 10 + 5 = 195.\n- Test 17 (loyalty): 100 - 20 + 10 + 5 = 95.\n- Test 18 (first insurance): same as test 2 now, 115.\n\nWait, test 18 becomes redundant with test 2. But that's OK, it verifies the first-insurance rule explicitly.\n\nNow I need to update the implementation to round premium up. Then update all tests.\n\nLet me add rounding.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:115","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { results: [{ premium }] };","newText":"  const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + loyaltyDiscount + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { results: [{ premium: Math.ceil(premium) }] };"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":5305,"output":1235,"cacheRead":75136,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1072,"totalTokens":81676,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":