s.bash:2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run src/claim-office.spec.ts\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (45 tests | 26 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  19 passed | 26 todo (45)\n   Start at  20:12:34\n   Duration  164ms (transform 32ms, setup 0ms, collect 32ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 43ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784923954483},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests pass. Now let me document the initial APP mass and naming evaluation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"**Rule 1 — Tests Pass**: Baseline confirmed — 19 tests passing, 26 todo.\n\n---\n\n### Naming Evaluation\n\n| Name | Purpose | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| `processScenario` | Orchestrates quote/claim steps | Clear |\n| `quotePremium` | Computes a single quote premium | Clear |\n| `premiumBreakdownForItems` | Separates policy base from item surcharges | Clear |\n| `basePremiumForItem` | Looks up base premium by item type | Clear |\n| `itemSurchargeFor` | Calculates curse/enchantment surcharges for one item | Clear |\n| `componentBasePremiumForCount` | Computes component block premium | Clear |\n| `loyaltyDiscountRateFor` | Loyalty discount rate (negative) based on customer | Clear |\n| `followUpDiscountRateFor` | Follow-up discount rate (negative) based on quote index | Clear |\n| `firstInsuranceSurchargeFor` | **Always returns 10%; parameter `_customer` is unused** | **Misleading** — name implies customer dependency, but it is constant |\n\n**Decision**: Remove `firstInsuranceSurchargeFor` and use the existing constant `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE` directly. This eliminates a misleading unused parameter (Rule 4) without harming intent (the constant name is self-documenting).\n\n---\n\n### Current APP Mass\n\nUsing APP counting rules (constants ×1, bindings ×1, invocations ×2, conditionals ×4, loops ×5, assignments ×6):\n\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD = 5;\nconst UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 100;\nconst COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 25;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\ntype Customer = { yearsWithMHPCO: number; };\ntype Step = { op?: string; items?: unknown[]; };\ntype ScenarioInput = { customer: Customer; steps: Step[]; };\ntype Item = { type?: string; cursed?: boolean; enchantment?: number; material?: string; };\ntype PremiumBreakdown = { policyBase: number; itemSurcharges: number; };\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: Item, basePremium: number): number => {\n  let rate = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) rate += CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    rate += HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  }\n  return basePremium * rate;\n};\n\nconst componentBasePremiumForCount = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK\n    ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst premiumBreakdownForItems = (items: Item[]): PremiumBreakdown => {\n  const componentCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const type = item.type ?? \"\";\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(type, (componentCounts.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n      policyBase += base;\n      itemSurcharges += itemSurchargeFor(item, base);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const count of componentCounts.values()) {\n    policyBase += componentBasePremiumForCount(count);\n  }\n\n  return { policyBase, itemSurcharges };\n};\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountRateFor = (customer: Customer): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? -LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (_customer: Customer): number => FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n\nconst followUpDiscountRateFor = (quoteIndex: number): number =>\n  quoteIndex > 0 ? -FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst quotePremium = (\n  customer: Customer,\n  items: Item[],\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): { premium: number } => {\n  const { policyBase, itemSurcharges } = premiumBreakdownForItems(items);\n  const policyWideRate =\n    loyaltyDiscountRateFor(customer) +\n    firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(customer) +\n    followUpDiscountRateFor(quoteIndex);\n  const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyBase * policyWideRate + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium) };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } => {\n  const input = scenario as ScenarioInput;\n  const results: Array<{ premium: number }> = [];\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n\n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const items = step.items ?? [];\n      results.push(quotePremium(input.customer, items as Item[], quoteIndex));\n      quoteIndex += 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\n**Component count:**\n- Constants: 20\n- Bindings: 47\n- Invocations: 12\n- Conditionals: 4\n- Loops: 3\n- Assignments: 8\n\n**Total Mass: 170**\n\nNow I'll apply the first refactoring: remove the unused-parameter function."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:3","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (_customer: Customer): number => FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n","newText":""},{"oldText":"    loyaltyDiscountRateFor(customer) +\n    firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(customer) +\n    followUpDiscountRateFor(quoteIndex);","newText":"    loyaltyDiscountRateFor(customer) +\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE +\n    followUpDiscountRateFor(quoteIndex);"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":262,"output":1486,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":16,"totalTokens":17876,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784923954483,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bdea3d69-bfd5-4dfc-9879-148f8b5e0f69","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:3","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  89 \n  90 const loyaltyDiscountRateFor = (customer: Customer): number =>\n  91   customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? -LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  92 \n- 93 const firstInsuranceSurchargeFor = (_customer: Customer): number => FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  94 \n  95 const followUpDiscountRateFor = (quoteIndex: number): number =>\n  96   quoteIndex > 0 ? -FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n  97 \n     ...\n 102 ): { premium: number } => {\n 103   const { policyBase, itemSurcharges } = premiumBreakdownForItems(items);\n 104   const policyWideRate =\n 105     loyaltyDiscountRateFor(customer) +\n-106     firstInsuranceSurchargeFor(customer) +\n+105     FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE +\n 107     followUpDiscountRateFor(quoteIndex);\n 108   const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharge