io` into `processQuoteStep` and `processClaimStep` so the main orchestrator reads as a clean dispatch loop.\n3. **Extract types**: Added `Damage` and `Incident` types to eliminate duplicated inline `{ itemType; amount }` shapes.\n4. **Tighten types**: Changed `Step.items` from `unknown[]` to `Item[]`, removing `as Item[]` casts.\n5. **Explaining variable**: Added `policyWideAdjustment` in `quotePremium` to clarify how the policy-wide rate contributes to the premium.\n6. **Type the public API**: Changed `processScenario(scenario: unknown)` to `processScenario(scenario: ScenarioInput)`, removing the `as ScenarioInput` cast.\n7. **Constant grouping**: Grouped constants by domain (quote/premium, item modifiers, customer modifiers, claim) with section comments.\n\n**APP Mass** (modified functions only):\n- Before: `processScenario` 75 + `processClaim` 24 + `reimbursementFor` 6 + `quotePremium` 17 = **122**\n- After: `processScenario` 47 + `processClaim` 24 + `reimbursementFor` 6 + `quotePremium` 18 + `processQuoteStep` 10 + `processClaimStep` 22 = **127**\n- Mass Change: **122 → 127 (+5)**\n\n**Why mass increased slightly**: Extracting two step-handler functions adds minimal function overhead, but `processScenario` mass dropped from 75 to 47. Per Rule 2, clarity trumps the small APP increase.\n\n**Tests**: All 26 passing tests remain green (`19 todo` unchanged)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 26\nRecent Green phase: Added policy creation, claim processing with deductible and cap tracking\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"te