e * (1 + policyWideRate)` introduces floating point error.\n\nI could use a different explaining variable that preserves math, like:\n```ts\nconst policyWideAdjustment = policyBase * policyWideRate;\nconst premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyWideAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n```\n\nThis keeps the same multiplication order and avoids the floating point issue. Let me revert to this.\n\nActually, the original `policyBase * policyWideRate` is already there. Adding `policyWideAdjustment` just renames/extracts it. This would add 1 binding but keep behavior.\n\nLet me revert and use this safer extraction.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring broke tests due to a floating-point precision change (`100 * 1.1` vs `100 * 0.1`). Reverting to a behavior-preserving extraction."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:14","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"  const adjustedBase = policyBase * (1 + policyWideRate);\n  const premium = adjustedBase + itemSurcharges + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium) };","newText":"  const policyWideAdjustment = policyBase * policyWideRate;\n  const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyWideAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium) };"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":2303,"output":889,"cacheRead":24064,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":719,"totalTokens":27256,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924167311,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7da96370-e599-4f93-8e5e-fd49814fc62c","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:14","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 130   const policyWideRate =\n 131     loyaltyDiscoun