or":true,"timestamp":1784924246385},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"## Red -- Test 29: should reimburse enchantment-8 damage at 50% then deductible -- 400 G for 1000 G damage\n\nRed Phase - Compilation Error Prediction:\n- Expected: No compilation error\n- Actual: No compilation error\n\nRed Phase - Runtime Error Prediction:\n- Expected: Assertion error, payout 900 vs 400\n- Reason: High-enchantment claim reimbursement rule not yet implemented\n- Actual: Assertion error as predicted\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected payout 400, received payout 900 Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected with assertion error\n\nProceeding to Green phase.\n\nGreen: implement high-enchantment claim rule. Need to look up the item's enchantment from the policy. The damage has itemType, and the policy has items. For each damage, find the matching insured item and use its enchantment/material.\n\nFor this test, one sword with enchantment 8. Damage amount 1000. Reimbursement = 1000 * 0.5 - 100 = 400.\n\nI need to update `reimbursementFor` to look up the item in the policy. For each damage, find an item of the same type. For multiple items of same type, we need to handle damage entries matching insured count. But for now, simple lookup.\n\nLet me implement:\n```typescript\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  const item = policy.items.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n  const enchantment = item?.enchantment ?? 0;\n  let amount = damage.amount;\n  if (enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    amount = amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return Math.max(0, amount - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD);\n};\n```\n\nBut this uses the first item of the type. For multiple items, we need to track which item is damaged. The damage entries don't specify which specific item, just type. The spec says each damage entry is treated as separate. For multiple items of same type, each damage entry consumes one insured item.\n\nFor now, this test has one item. I'll implement simple lookup.\n\nAlso need dragon material full reimbursement. Let me add that too since upcoming tests need it.\n\n```typescript\nconst DRAGON_MATERIAL = \"dragon\";\n\nconst reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  const item = policy.items.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);\n  const enchantment = item?.enchantment ?? 0;\n  const material = item?.material ?? \"\";\n  let amount = damage.amount;\n  if (enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    amount = amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  } else if (material === DRAGON_MATERIAL) {\n    // full reimbursement, amount unchanged\n  }\n  return Math.max(0, amount - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD);\n};\n```\n\nWait, the spec says \"Damage to items made of dragon material is fully reimbursed.\" And \"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (both clauses apply; the 50 % rule wins, then deductible: 500 − 100)\". So high enchantment wins over dragon material. The else if is correct: if enchantment >= 8, apply 50%; else if dragon, full.\n\nBut what about a dragon-material item with enchantment < 8? Full reimbursement.\n\nLet me implement.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:153","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;","newText":"const DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst DRAGON_MATERIAL = \"dragon\";"},{"oldText":"const reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  return Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD);\n};","newText":"const reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  const item = policy.items.find((policyItem) => policyItem.type === damage.itemType);\n  const enchantment = item?.enchantment ?? 0;\n  const material = item?.material ?? \"\";\n  let amount = damage.amount;\n  if (enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    amount *= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  } else if (material === DRAGON_MATERIAL) {\n    // full reimbursement, amount unchanged\n  }\n  return Math.max(0, amount - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD);\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":687,"output":1149,"cacheRead":107264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":787,"totalTokens":109100,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924246388,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ba5a2c8e-01c6-45af-8c40-7678ad06adce","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:153","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  26 \n  27 // Claim constants\n  28 const DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD = 100;\n  29 const CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n+ 30 const HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\n+ 31 const HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n+ 32 const DRAGON_MATERIAL = \"dragon\";\n  30 const INSURANCE_VALUES_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  31   sword: 1000,\n  32   amulet: 600,\n  33   staff: 800,\n     ...\n 148   return { insuranceSum, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CAP_MULTIPLIER, items };\n 149 };\n 150 \n 151 const reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n-152   return Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE_