ow reads as a clean pipeline: find item → adjust damage → subtract deductible.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Removed the misleading `else if (material === DRAGON_MATERIAL)` branch that performed no work. Replaced it with a comment that explicitly states dragon-material items receive full reimbursement by default.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: The high-enchantment check now lives in exactly one place.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Removed the now-unused `DRAGON_MATERIAL` constant.\n- **Side effect**: Eliminated the mutable `let amount` variable inside `reimbursementFor`, making the function pure.\n\n**Tests**: All 29 passing tests remain green; 16 todo tests unchanged.\n\nRefactoring Complete."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 29\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment and dragon-material claim reimbursement rules\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 29\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment and dragon-material claim reimbursement rules\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784924270142},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to refactor the implementation. I need to first read the relevant files to understand the code, then apply refactoring principles. Let me read the test file and implementation file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.