ch claim, so remainingCap wouldn't be tracked across claims. I need to update the policy's remainingCap after each claim.\n\nThe current processClaim returns a new ClaimResult but doesn't mutate policy. I need to mutate policy.remainingCap or return updated policy.\n\nLet me run test first to confirm failure.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.bash:182","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":103,"output":141,"cacheRead":122112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":123,"totalTokens":122356,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924526294,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-839c51fe-e550-464a-bac5-e6203f219821","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.bash:182","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (45 tests | 1 failed | 7 skipped) 12ms\n   ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should reduce payout to remaining cap on second claim -- 600 G remaining\n     → expected { results: [ { premium: 115 }, …(2) ] } to deeply equal { results: [ { premium: 115 }, …(2) ] }\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯ Failed Tests 1 ⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯\n\n FAIL  src/claim-office.spec.ts > MHPCO Claim Office > should reduce payout to remaining cap on second claim -- 600 G remaining\nAssertionError: expected { results: [ { premium: 115 }, …(2) ] } to deeply equal { results: [ { premium: 115 }, …(2) ] }\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n  Object {\n    \"results\": Array [\n      Object {\n        \"premium\": 115,\n      },\n      Object {\n        \"payout\": 1400,\n        \"remainingCap\": 600,\n      },\n      Object {\n-       \"payout\": 600,\n-       \"remainingCap\": 0,\n+       \"payout\": 1400,\n+       \"remainingCap\": 600,\n      },\n    ],\n  }\n\n ❯ src/claim-office.spec.ts:565:20\n    563|       ],\n    564|     });\n    565|     expect(result).toEqual({\n       |                    ^\n    566|       results: [\n    567|         { premium: 115 },\n\n⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯⎯[1/1]⎯\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 37 passed | 7 todo (45)\n   Start at  20:22:09\n   Duration  193ms (transform 41ms, setup 0ms, collect 41ms, tests 12ms, environment 0ms, prepare 49ms)\n\n ELIFECYCLE  Test failed. See above for more details.\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784924529439},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"## Red -- Test 38: should reduce payout to remaining cap on second claim -- 600 G remaining\n\nRed Phase - Compilation Error Prediction:\n- Expected: No compilation error\n- Actual: No compilation error\n\nRed Phase - Runtime Error Prediction:\n- Expected: Assertion error, second claim payout 1400 vs 600\n- Reason: Policy remainingCap is not updated after first claim\n- Actual: Assertion error as predicted\n\nRed Phase Complete:\n**Compilation Prediction**: No compilation error Correct\n**Runtime Prediction**: Expected second claim payout 600, received 1400 Correct\n**Result**: Test fails as expected with assertion error\n\nProceeding to Green phase.\n\nGreen: update policy.remainingCap after claim. Modify processClaim to mutate policy or return updated policy. I'll mutate the policy object.\n\n```typescript\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementFor(damage, policy), 0);\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  policy.remainingCap -= roundedPayout;\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};\n```\n\nNeed to update processClaimStep since it receives policy from Map. Mutating it will persist.\n\nLet me implement.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:183","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  let totalPayout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    totalPayout += reimbursementFor(damage, policy);\n  }\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - roundedPayout };\n};","newText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementFor(damage, policy),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  policy.remainingCap -= roundedPayout;\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":683,"output":609,"cacheRead":122304,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":292,"totalTokens":123596,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924529443,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e9de43e9-720a-4e2a-98e9-b2890732ba7a","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.edit:183","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Could not find the exact text in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts. The old text must match exactly including all whitespace and newlines."}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1784924535091},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The subagent may have already refactored processClaim. Let me read.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:184","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":99,"output":81,"cacheRead":123584,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":123764,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784924535094,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7b319802-f0b7-4015-8e0b-bca4cc9752b8","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:184","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Quote / premium constants\nconst PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD = 5;\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\nconst UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 100;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD = 25;\n\n// Item modifier constants\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\n\n// Customer modifier constants\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\n// Claim constants\nconst DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES_GOLD: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ntype Customer = {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n};\n\ntype Step = {\n  op?: string;\n  items?: Item[];\n  policy?: number;\n  incident?: Incident;\n};\n\ntype ScenarioInput = {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\ntype Item = {\n  type?: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  material?: string;\n};\n\ntype PremiumBreakdown = {\n  policyBase: number;\n  itemSurcharges: number;\n};\n\ntype Damage = {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n};\n\ntype Incident = {\n  damages: Damage[];\n};\n\ntype Policy = {\n  insuranceSum: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n  items: Item[];\n};\n\ntype QuoteResult = { premium: number };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\ntype Result = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  BASE_PREMIUMS_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? UNKNOWN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst itemSurchargeFor = (item: Item, basePremium: number): number => {\n  const curseRate = item.cursed ? CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const enchantmentRate =\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD\n      ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return basePremium * (curseRate + enchantmentRate);\n};\n\nconst componentBasePremiumForCount = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK\n    ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_GOLD;\n\nconst premiumBreakdownForItems = (items: Item[]): PremiumBreakdown => {\n  const componentCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const type = item.type ?? \"\";\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(type)) {\n      componentCounts.set(type, (componentCounts.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n    } else {\n      const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n      policyBase += base;\n      itemSurcharges += itemSurchargeFor(item, base);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const count of componentCounts.values()) {\n    policyBase += componentBasePremiumForCount(count);\n  }\n\n  return { policyBase, itemSurcharges };\n};\n\nconst loyaltyDiscountRateFor = (customer: Customer): number =>\n  customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? -LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst followUpDiscountRateFor = (quoteIndex: number): number =>\n  quoteIndex > 0 ? -FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0;\n\nconst quotePremium = (customer: Customer, items: Item[], quoteIndex: number): QuoteResult => {\n  const { policyBase, itemSurcharges } = premiumBreakdownForItems(items);\n  const policyWideRate =\n    loyaltyDiscountRateFor(customer) +\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE +\n    followUpDiscountRateFor(quoteIndex);\n  const policyWideAdjustment = policyBase * policyWideRate;\n  const premium = policyBase + itemSurcharges + policyWideAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE_GOLD;\n  return { premium: Math.ceil(premium) };\n};\n\nconst createPolicy = (items: Item[]): Policy => {\n  const insuranceSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + (INSURANCE_VALUES_GOLD[item.type ?? \"\"] ?? 0),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { insuranceSum, remainingCap: insuranceSum * CAP_MULTIPLIER, items };\n};\n\nconst adjustedDamageFor = (item: Item | undefined, amount: number): number => {\n  const enchantment = item?.enchantment ?? 0;\n  if (enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    return amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  // Items below the high-enchantment threshold are reimbursed at the full damage amount.\n  return amount;\n};\n\nconst reimbursementFor = (damage: Damage, policy: Policy): number => {\n  const item = policy.items.find((policyItem) => policyItem.type === damage.itemType);\n  const adjustedAmount = adjustedDamageFor(item, damage.amount);\n  return Math.max(0, adjustedAmount - DEDUCTIBLE_GOLD);\n};\n\nconst countByKey = <T>(items: T[], keyExtractor: (item: T) => string): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const key = keyExtractor(item);\n    counts.set(key, (counts.get(key) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst itemCountsByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> =>\n  countByKey(items, (item) => item.type ?? \"\");\n\nconst damageCountsByType = (damages: Damage[]): Map<string, number> =>\n  countByKey(damages, (damage) => damage.itemType);\n\nconst validateClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): void => {\n  const policyCounts = itemCountsByType(policy.items);\n  const damageCounts = damageCountsByType(incident.damages);\n  for (const [type, count] of damageCounts.entries()) {\n    if ((policyCounts.get(type) ?? 0) < count) {\n      throw new Error(`Claim damages exceed insured count for ${type}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementFor(damage, policy),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - roundedPayout };\n};\n\nconst processQuoteStep = (\n  step: Step,\n  customer: Customer,\n  quoteIndex: number,\n): { result: QuoteResult; policy: Policy } => {\n  const items = step.items ?? [];\n  const policy = createPolicy(items);\n  return {\n    result: quotePremium(customer, items, quoteIndex),\n    policy,\n  };\n};\n\nconst processClaimStep = (\n  step: Step,\n  policies: Map<number, Policy>,\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const policy = policies.get(step.policy ?? -1);\n  if (!policy || !step.incident) {\n    return { payout: 0, remainingCap: 0 };\n  }\n  return processClaim(policy, step.incident);\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: ScenarioInput): { results: Result[] } => {\n  const results: Result[] = [];\n  const policies = new Map<number, Policy>();\n  let quoteIndex = 0;\n\n  for (const [stepIndex, step] of scenario.steps.entries()) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const { result, policy } = processQuoteStep(step, scenario.customer, quoteIndex);\n      policies.set(stepIndex, policy);\n      results.push(result);\n      quoteIndex += 1;\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      results.push(processClaimStep(step, policies));\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784924536741},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to update processClaim to mutate remainingCap. Let me edit.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.edit:185","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-37-06_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementFor(damage, policy),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap - roundedPayout };\n};","newText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  validateClaim(policy, incident);\n  const totalPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementFor(damage, policy),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.min(totalPayout, policy.remainingCap);\n  const roundedPayout = Math.floor(payout);\n  policy.remainingCap -= roundedPayout;\n  return { payout: roundedPayout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};"}]}}],"api":